---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const pageSections = [
  { id: 'about-intro', label: 'Introduction' },
  { id: 'about-story', label: 'Story' },
  { id: 'about-principles', label: 'How I work' },
] as const;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | Joel Rhine"
  description="Joel Rhine is a software engineer and product builder with a background in coffee, operations, and field leadership, focused on making tools that work for the people using them."
  pageSections={pageSections}
>
  <header id="about-intro" class="page-intro" data-od-id="about-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">About Joel</p><h1>
      I came to software through the people the work depends on.
    </h1>
  </header>
  <article id="about-story" class="prose" data-od-id="about-story">
    <p>
      Before software, I worked in coffee, wholesale, logistics, and field
      leadership. Those jobs made the cost of a bad process easy to see. A
      confusing tool means lost time, missed handoffs, unhappy customers, or
      extra work for the person stuck carrying it.
    </p>
    <p>
      I moved into software in 2018 and joined Honey in 2020. I worked on
      merchant integrations, scraping configuration, operational dashboards, and
      on-call systems. At ZeroClick.ai, I worked on automations, retailer
      integrations, experiments, and internal engineering workflows.
    </p>
    <p>
      Today, I am building measure.coffee as its Founding Engineer. It brings
      together my coffee background and the software questions I care about: how
      people learn, make decisions, and get the help they need without extra
      friction.
    </p>
    <h2>What I bring to a team</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>An operator's attention to the actual workflow</li><li>
        Engineering experience across integrations, automation, and product
        systems
      </li><li>
        A practical approach to communication, collaboration, and handoff
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button button-primary" href="/files/resume.pdf"
        >Download resume</a
      >
    </div>
  </article>
  <section id="about-principles" class="section" data-od-id="about-principles">
    <header class="section-header compact section-header-canary">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">How I work</p><h2>How I work</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        I start with the people, study the work around them, make the system
        easier to understand, and leave it in good shape for the next person.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="principles">
      <article>
        <span class="micro" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <h3>Start with the people</h3><p>
          Look for repeated steps, workarounds people accept as normal, and the
          moments where someone needs help, clarity, or a faster path.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="micro" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
        <h3>Understand the work</h3><p>
          A complex system should not make everyday tasks harder for the person
          relying on it.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="micro" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
        <h3>Build something people want to use</h3><p>
          Good work is easier to maintain, explain, and extend when another
          person has to pick it up.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
